## Commits

Format: `{{commit_pattern}}` <!-- GEN: default `type(TICKET): summary` -->

| Type | Use for | Version effect |
|---|---|---|
| `feat` | New behavior | MINOR |
| `fix` | Bug fix | PATCH |
| `perf` | Performance without behavior change | PATCH |
| `refactor`, `chore`, `docs`, `test` | No behavior change | none alone |
| `type!` or footer `BREAKING CHANGE:` | Breaks a contract ([05]({{ref_05}})) | MAJOR |

Check: `{{commit_check_cmd}}` <!-- GEN: e.g. npx commitlint --from origin/develop --to HEAD; "none" if the repo has no tool -->

One PR = one ticket or logical change. Never commit secrets; never bypass hooks with `--no-verify`.

